# E19 Why key smoothing matters on some models (pipeline check + characterization)

**TL;DR:** pipeline check (offline exact attention vs the model's own o_proj input), max rel. error: qwen3.5-0.8b 0.014, qwen3.5-2b 0.012, qwen3-0.6b 0.006.
Median predicted smoothing gain (Σq²·Σk²/(Σ√(q²k²))², from prefill stats): qwen3.5-0.8b 1.34x, qwen3.5-2b 1.29x, qwen3-0.6b 4.09x;
measured 2-bit logit-MSE gain: qwen3.5-0.8b 1.21x, qwen3.5-2b 1.20x, qwen3-0.6b 3.41x (Spearman predicted vs measured over heads 0.97).

## Config
Reference per model: {'qwen3.5-0.8b': 'int8', 'qwen3.5-2b': 'int8', 'qwen3-0.6b': 'fp16'}. Corpora ['prose', 'code']; up to 4 attention layers per model; all KV heads; 2-bit (coarse) gain-shape keys with 128-token block means.
Logit error is measured on every 4th decode query over all causal positions. k² = per-channel variance of post-RoPE prefill keys,
q² = per-channel mean square of post-RoPE prefill queries (averaged over the GQA group). runtime 131s.

